  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Yusuf. You're verified.\n\n**Order K-6601 (Spice Route):** Spice Route has an open incident tonight. A sauce batch used in their curries was recalled by the supplier, and your order was placed during the time it covers. Because of that, I can't refund or credit this order myself. Forkful's incident team handles compensation for every affected order, so I've sent your case to them, including the wrong item (chicken makhani instead of paneer makhani). A specialist will contact you within 24 hours. Your reference number is **ESC-700**.\n\nSince curries are involved in the recall, please don't eat the curry from this order. I'm glad nobody did. If anyone feels unwell after eating anything from it, tell me right away.\n\nWhat went wrong with your other orders?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, a recall? Nobody mentioned that to me, and I'm not sure what to do with that. Are the other curries from Spice Route safe to eat, or is it only certain ones? And will I still get the money back for this order? I really just want my card refunded.\n\nAnyway, the second Spice Route order, #6602, was a small one I placed a few minutes after the first for extra naan. One of the two garlic naans was missing."
